  "definitions": {
    "adherence_denominator": "First3/first4: all200 episodes. Later positions: only episodes still producing that query; this survivor selection is explicit. Empty-note arms have no own-note adherence, but are compared to E opening patterns.",
    "capped25": "Recorded first singleton turn when resolved, otherwise 25; a successful turn-25 episode has same cost as a cap failure.",
    "curves": "Candidate counts use recorded after values. After early identification, carry forward one remaining candidate to turn25. log2 cardinality is a descriptive uncertainty-size proxy, not measured model entropy.",
    "duplicate_query": "A recorded guess exactly repeats any earlier guess in that episode.",
    "invalid_and_truncation": "Missing/non-four-ASCII-digit recorded guess and finish_reason=length counted separately. Repeated-digit four-character queries are separately described; no explicit invalid flag exists in episode schema, so these are not relabelled as parser failures.",
    "no_information": "Existing monitor after==before; no new candidate filtering or hidden-label access is performed.",
    "request_byte_comparison": "Canonical UTF-8 serialization of complete six-key request objects in call_intent. Exact messages/scalars match; original HTTP byte streams were not captured and are not claimed identical.",
    "resolved": "Recorded monitor reached a singleton candidate set, not necessarily actor emitted the correct secret.",
    "shared_resolved": "Case pairing occurs privately in memory. Intersection of resolved cases is outcome-selected; its speed contrast is descriptive, not a causally identified effect."
  },
